But why wouldn't they stack in the first place? That would mean that 
before identification, they were different, which they weren't. The only 
reason I can think of is that he picked up one, identified it, then 
picked up the other and identified it. With the last ID, the scroll 
would have stayed in the same slot is already was in.

By the way, I don't consider this a bug. You may have a preferred slot 
for identify scrolls, which may be either H or N. The interface could 
never determine which one you prefer.

> In such a case you have to drop the items.

Not necessarily. Dropping them and picking them up again means losing 
two turns, which in some cases (like a speed ascension) may be a 
problem.

The simpler way, which costs NO turns, is to #adjust slot H to any 
letter (which may be H). The N items will automagically merge.

